  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> lies on <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0,</mn></math>&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi></math> lies on <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is a rhombus, then the locus of <math><mi>D</mi></math> is a conic whose length of the latus rectum is equal to"
